                  "uri": "internal/defaults/defaults.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 93,
                  "startLine": 82
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "The only control that keeps tenant defaults out of protected namespaces is an exact name-prefix check at enqueue time (default -skip-prefixes=\"kube-\"). The informer registers its AddFunc before Run, so client-go replays the initial LIST of all Active namespaces as Add events on every controller start, and the namespace \"default\" plus any add-on or system-like namespace whose name does not begin with \"kube-\" (for example istio-system, ingress-nginx, kubernetes-dashboard) is stamped with a fixed production-quota ResourceQuota and a max-capped LimitRange. The injection is sticky because sync tolerates AlreadyExists and never updates or removes existing objects."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:fc95d36b0bb109942a67dc0309e58eb03081ae0434e646d41d2e1fc06f76548a",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "77879c21520b058e:1"
          },
